// `main` returns the exit status, `fn uint8 main()` (and `fn uint32 main()` on Windows). A `fn void main()` used to pass `kama check` and then fail in
// clang on the synthesized `return (int)kama_main();` — accepted by kama, refused by the C compiler.
import { core::println };
fn void main() { println(s: "never built"); }
